  },
  {
    "source": "Lisa Barlow, who has the most opportunities to apologize, but seems to be the worst at it.",
    "why": "Identifying Lisa Barlow as having the most apology opportunities and the worst record requires per-cast counts and classifications, but apologies.csv has no cast-member column."
  },
  {
    "source": "A chart showing 91 episodes of The Real Housewives of Salt Lake City with markings where the apology moments occur.",
    "why": "episodes.csv lists 94 episodes, and the apology log covers 80 distinct episodes, so the chart's 91-episode figure is not reproduced by the files."
  },
  {
    "source": "We can tell the apologies don’t work because the same issues resurface in the next episode, again and again.",
    "why": "No field marks repeated issues or links an apology moment to a later recurrence, so the claimed recurrence pattern cannot be computed from the files."
  },
  {
    "source": "The final step of actually facing the thing you apologized for, bettering yourself, and being different rarely occurs.",
    "why": "No field records post-apology follow-through or changed behavior, so the claim that follow-through rarely occurs cannot be computed from the files."
  }
]

